{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082246Z_dev-05_flat_47c2", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not give a detection significance for the GCE, in σ or as a test statistic. It only says that the fitted GCE flux stays nonzero across all 80 diffuse-emission models. It adds that this \"alone does not establish its statistical significance.\" It also says the Δ(−2lnL) differences between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The only fit statistics it reports are χ² values for the dark-matter spectral fits. For example, χ²_min = 27.50 for 12 degrees of freedom in the b b̄ channel.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}]}, "turns": 2, "seconds": 4.155, "tool_calls": 1, "tool_result_chars": 147086, "input_tokens": 6, "output_tokens": 364, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 67327, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:22:50+00:00"}
